# diff-lower rulings (tests/differential/settle.zig): a fixture where the LRM
# sides with Sema's lowering and not the old one (src/analog).
# `<path> | <clause> | new | <expected> | <why>`. <expected> is the new side's
# codes, comma-separated and sorted, when the codes differ; when the tables
# differ, their difference: `-<old row>` for each old row the new side lacks,
# then `+<new row>` for each new row the old lacks, joined by `; `. The clause
# is one the fixture's `//! lrm` lines cite. A ruling that settles nothing
# fails the run.
verilog-a/ch03_data_types/integer_conversion_saturates.va | 4.2.1.1 | new | -param big integer = 1e300; +param big integer = ? | §4.2.1.1 a real assigned where an integer is required "shall be converted to an integer by rounding", and §3.4.1 makes `parameter integer` the 32-bit type: no integer is 1e300, so the old row's folded default is no value of the parameter's type; the new side leaves the default unfolded (the fixture's saturated 2147483647 is the device's to compute)
verilog-a/ch06_hierarchy/generate_if_instantiates_one_arm.va | 6.6.2 | new | -display $strobe | §6.6 "At most one generate block instantiated from a set of alternatives" (elab.rulings drops `on.u_on`): the old side lowers the unselected arm's instance too, with its `$strobe`
verilog-a/ch06_hierarchy/paramset_defparam_hierarchy_legal.va | 6.6.2 | new | -contrib flow direct br4 sum_node gnd; -contrib flow direct br5 sum_node gnd | §6.6.2 instantiates only a selected arm (elab.rulings drops `absent` and `valid.absent_child`): the old side lowers both dropped instances, and each contributes a flow into `sum_node`
verilog-a/ch09_system_tasks/reject_simprobe_runtime_name.va | 9.16 | new | E0823 | §9.16 lets inst_name be "a string variable", whose value exists only when the analog block runs; VerA resolves names at compile time (specification/Vague_Decisions.md VD-030), so it refuses the call with E0823, fallback or not (the fixture's `//! reject-only E0823`), where the old side builds a select chain over the siblings
verilog-a/ch10_directives/compact_modeling_macro_implies_its_extensions.va | 10.5 | new | -held fold | `fold[nslot - 1]` is written before it is read in the same run of the analog block, so no value crosses a step and nothing is held; the old side does not fold the localparam subscript and holds the whole array
verilog-ams/annex_a_syntax/specparam_range_and_select.va | A.2.1.1 | new | -param wrap integer local = 21; +param wrap integer local = 5 | A.2.1.1 `specparam [ range ]`, and IEEE 1364-2005 §4.10.3 (inherited): "A specparam with a range specification shall be the range of the parameter declaration": `[3:0]` keeps 21's low 4 bits, 5, where the old side keeps 21
verilog-ams/ch07_mixed_signal/driver_state_histogram.va | 9.22.3 | new | -held net__m04_ds_c2e__ddiscrete.n; -held net__m04_ds_c2e__ddiscrete.ones; -held net__m04_ds_c2e__ddiscrete.zeros; -held net__m04_ds_c2e__ddiscrete.xs; -held net__m04_ds_c2e__ddiscrete.zs | the §9.22.3 histogram is counted by the connect module's digital `initial` (§7.2.2: a variable a digital process writes is the digital context's), which the analog block never writes, so no analog held row is its; the old side holds them as analog variables
verilog-ams/ch07_mixed_signal/driver_update_without_resolved_change.va | 9.22.3 | new | -held net__m04_du_c2e__ddiscrete.ones | the §9.22.3 count is kept by the connect module's digital process (§7.2.2: the digital context's variable), which the analog block never writes, so no analog held row is its; the old side holds it as an analog variable
verilog-ams/ch09_system_tasks/stochastic_queue_in_digital_context.va | 9.9 | new | -held st | §9.9 leaves the IEEE 1364 §17.6 queue tasks to the digital context: `st` is only the status output of `$q_*` calls in an `initial` block, never written by the analog block, so it is no analog held row; the old side holds it
verilog-a/ch06_hierarchy/if_generate_values_drive_paramset_selection.va | 6.9.2 | new | -display $strobe; -display $strobe; -display $strobe | §6.9.2 "paramset selection is performed after the generate construct has been evaluated" (elab.rulings drops `g1.u2` and `g2.u3`): the old side lowers the two unselected arms' instances too, the wide one's two `$strobe`s and the narrow one's one
verilog-a/ch06_hierarchy/paramset_selected_by_generate_localparam.va | 6.6.2 | new | -param w1 real local = 1e1; -param w2 real local = 1e0; -param w3 real local = 1e1; -param w4 real local = 1e0; -param w real local = 1e0 | §6.6.2 a generate block is a scope of its own, and only the selected arm is instantiated: `w2` and `w3` are in arms that do not exist (elab.rulings drops `g1.u2` and `g2.u3`), and `w1`, `w4` and `w` are `g1`'s and `g2`'s, folded into the instance overrides that read them; the old side lists all five as the module's own parameters
